phs) in Azerbaijan [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobustan_Rock_Art_Cultural_Landscape]; The engravings show lance-bearers and ritual dance scenes [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobustan_Rock_Art_Cultural_Landscape]; The engravings show camel caravans [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobustan_Rock_Art_Cultural_Landscape]; The engravings show the sun and other stars [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobustan_Rock_Art_Cultural_Landscape]; The rock art was discovered by quarry workers in the 1930s [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobustan_Rock_Art_Cultural_Landscape]; The engravings date from prehistoric to medieval times [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gobustan_Rock_Art_Cultural_Landscape]; The site shows human use from the Upper Paleolithic to the Middle Ages (UNESCO) [SUPPORTED, no proving quote: https://whc.unesco.org/en/list/1076]"}]'::jsonb),
