09-27-04/OUTCOMES.jsonl", "quote": "The Roman Ruins of Pisões are a Roman villa rustica (a farming villa) in the Beja municipality of Portugal, the central claim about what and where the site is [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ruins_of_Pis%C3%B5es]; Mosaics with geometrical and naturalistic motifs decorate the main (more important) rooms of the villa [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ruins_of_Pis%C3%B5es]; The villa was a farm that supplied the city of Pax Julia with foodstuffs [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ruins_of_Pis%C3%B5es]; A Roman dam lies near the villa [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ruins_of_Pis%C3%B5es]; The villa was supplied with water from the nearby Roman dam [SUPPORTED: https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_ruins_of_Pis%C3%B5es]"}]'::jsonb),
